# The dock is the 24-cell, DERIVED from the tone. Four slots each hold a tone, so there are 3^4 = 81 tetrads (vibe/dock).
# Count them by how many slots hold a vibe: a calm slot contributes 1 and each of the two vibes contributes x, so one
# slot is 1 + 2x and four slots are (1 + 2x)^4. The coefficient of x^k is the number of tetrads with k vibes:
#
#   (1 + 2x)^4 = 1 + 8 x + 24 x^2 + 32 x^3 + 16 x^4,    1 + 8 + 24 + 32 + 16 = 81 = 3^4.
#
# The shells are the origin, the 16-cell's 8 vertices +-e_i, the 24-cell's 24 vertices +-e_i +-e_j, 32 vectors with
# three vibes, and the tesseract's 16 vertices (+-1, +-1, +-1, +-1). The two-vibe shell is the only one that is a
# self-dual regular polytope, and it is the dock: vibe/dock proves those 24 tetrads are exactly the 24 Hurwitz units,
# with 12 lines and 3 frames. The same expansion with one choice per slot, (1 + x)^4 = 1 + 4x + 6x^2 + 4x^3 + x^4,
# counts the blades of the Clifford algebra Cl(4) by grade (vibe/clifford), and its even part 1 + 6 + 1 = 8 is the
# register a member carries.
#
# Proved as polynomial identities in x, for every x, so each coefficient is pinned, not only the total.

# What one slot contributes: calm counts 1, each of love and fear counts x.
task slot-weight
  take x, like integer
  like integer
  send back
    call add
      code 1
      call multiply
        code 2
        read x

task blade-weight
  take x, like integer
  like integer
  send back
    call add
      code 1
      read x

task fourth-power
  take y, like integer
  like integer
  send back
    call multiply
      call multiply
        read y
        read y
      call multiply
        read y
        read y

task power-of-x
  take x, like integer
  take c0, like integer
  take c1, like integer
  take c2, like integer
  take c3, like integer
  take c4, like integer
  like integer
  send back
    call add
      read c0
      call multiply
        read x
        call add
          read c1
          call multiply
            read x
            call add
              read c2
              call multiply
                read x
                call add
                  read c3
                  call multiply
                    read x
                    read c4

# THE SHELLS OF THE TONE: four slots of (1 + 2x) expand to 1 + 8x + 24x^2 + 32x^3 + 16x^4.
rule the-tetrads-split-into-shells-of-one-eight-twenty-four-thirty-two-sixteen
  seat x, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call fourth-power
        call slot-weight
          read x
      call power-of-x
        read x
        code 1
        code 8
        code 24
        code 32
        code 16

# ALL 81: at x = 1 every tetrad counts once, (1 + 2)^4 = 3^4.
rule the-shells-total-three-to-the-fourth
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call fourth-power
        call slot-weight
          code 1
      call fourth-power
        code 3

# THE BLADES OF Cl(4) BY GRADE: 1, 4, 6, 4, 1, sixteen in all, the even ones 1 + 6 + 1 = 8.
rule the-blades-split-by-grade-into-one-four-six-four-one
  seat x, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call fourth-power
        call blade-weight
          read x
      call power-of-x
        read x
        code 1
        code 4
        code 6
        code 4
        code 1

# Half the sum of (1 + x)^4 at x = 1 and x = -1 counts the even grades: (16 + 0) / 2 = 8.
rule the-even-blades-number-eight
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call add
        call fourth-power
          call blade-weight
            code 1
        call fourth-power
          call blade-weight
            code -1
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 8
